      "side": 1,
      "message": "The JNDI protocol does not give specifics on this [1], as you say, this is down to the provider implementations for different JDKs.\n\nIt used to be documented up to Java 8 [2], but I cannot find any specific documentation on more recent versions of Java or any specific distribution.\n\nI can see from the `openjdk` implementation (which the majority of java distributions are based on) that the space-separated URLs are still supported [3], but this is not officially documented anywhere.\n\n\nI will try to clarify this.\n\n[1] https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.naming/javax/naming/Context.html#PROVIDER_URL\n\n[2] https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/technotes/guides/jndi/jndi-ldap-gl.html#protocol\n\n[3] https://github.com/openjdk/jdk/blob/master/src/jdk.naming.dns/share/classes/com/sun/jndi/dns/DnsUrl.java#L89",
